{"id": "86113", "name": "כפולה משותפת מינימלית של שני מספרים (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "functions": [{"name": "ex", "params": ["m", "p"], "body": "if mod(m,p)#0 then 0 else 1+ex(m/p,p)"}], "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Find the Lowest Common Multiple (LCM) of \\({{CT:0}}\\) and \\({{CT:1}}\\).</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(\\text{LCM}=\\) [[input:ans]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Factorise both numbers into primes. The LCM is the product of all the primes that appear in either number, each with the higher of its two powers (a prime that appears in both is counted once, with its higher power).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Prime factorisation of both numbers</b><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}={{CT:2}} \\]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:1}}={{CT:3}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The higher power of each prime</b><br>For every prime that appears, compare its power in the two numbers (a prime that does not appear has power \\(0\\)) and take the higher one:<table dir=\"ltr\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px auto\"><tr><th style=\"padding:3px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid #4b1f6f\">prime</th><th style=\"padding:3px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid #4b1f6f\">power in \\({{CT:0}}\\)</th><th style=\"padding:3px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid #4b1f6f\">power in \\({{CT:1}}\\)</th><th style=\"padding:3px 12px;border-bottom:2px solid #4b1f6f\">higher power</th></tr>[[if test=\"{{CT:18}}\"]]<tr><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\(2\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\({{CT:4}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\({{CT:5}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\"><b>\\({{CT:6}}\\)</b></td></tr>[[/if]][[if test=\"{{CT:19}}\"]]<tr><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\(3\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\({{CT:7}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\({{CT:8}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\"><b>\\({{CT:9}}\\)</b></td></tr>[[/if]][[if test=\"{{CT:20}}\"]]<tr><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\(5\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\({{CT:10}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\({{CT:11}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\"><b>\\({{CT:12}}\\)</b></td></tr>[[/if]][[if test=\"{{CT:21}}\"]]<tr><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\(7\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\({{CT:13}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\">\\({{CT:14}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:3px 12px;text-align:center\"><b>\\({{CT:15}}\\)</b></td></tr>[[/if]]</table></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — Multiply</b><br>The LCM is the product of the primes with these higher powers:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\text{LCM}({{CT:0}},{{CT:1}})={{CT:16}}={{CT:17}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "factor", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "1-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "a*b", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-T (taken product by mistake)", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">You appear to have counted factors appearing in both {{CT:22}} and {{CT:23}} twice. By doing this you have simply found the product of {{CT:22}} and {{CT:23}}. The Lowest Common Multiple is only ever the product of two numbers if those two numbers are co-prime.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["a", "b", "g", "ta", "u", "v"], "nvariants": 50}